# Build context exclusions. `COPY . .` is only safe with this file present.
#
# The first entry is the important one: without it the image carries .env, and
# an image layer is readable by anyone who can pull it. Secrets reach the
# container from the host's secret store at runtime, never from a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime state. The relational store is the system of record and lives on a
# mounted volume; baking a copy into the image means a machine whose mount
# failed would quietly serve stale demo data instead of failing loudly.
data/
*.db
*.sqlite3

# Local-only working files (also gitignored) — nothing in the image should
# depend on them, and they are not the deployed product's business.
plan.md
handoff.md
problem_statement_*.md
retrieval-explained.md
patterns-explained.md
test-scenarios.md
spec-lessons-learned.html

# Weight with no purpose in the image.
.venv/
venv/
.git/
.github/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
